WEBVTT

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.960
The second group is...

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.170
What an amazing aura.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:57.920
Yeah.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.430
It's a miracle.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:02.470
Huh?

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:06.890
According to rumors, they were expected to win the award.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:08.810
What? Really?

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.900
I've heard that rumor too.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:15.360
Be that as it may, we will not give up.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:20.070
Yes. That is why we've been nominated.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:21.990
A miracle, huh?

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.950
In other words, we're on the same level as them.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.410
Yes.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:30.920
Let's switch our cameras over to HE☆VENS' concert hall!

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.420
Here they come!

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:40.840
The members of HE☆VENS, nominated for the Uta☆Pri Award, have arrived!

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.910
Amazing.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.240
Congratulations on your nomination.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:08.910
Tell our audience watching on TV how you're feeling right now.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.460
I'm HE☆VENS' Otori Eiichi.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.500
This nomination is truly upsetting.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.920
Is there anything else I could say?

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.050
No, of course not.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:25.260
What do you mean by that?

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.350
It's unthinkable to compare us to someone else.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.310
Isn't that right, angels?

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.650
Kira! Over here!

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.650
Kira, say something. It'll never be my turn if you don't.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.620
I am HE☆VENS' Sumeragi Kira.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.290
Kira, you're so wonderful!

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.290
You never say much, do you?

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:57.210
I'm HE☆VENS' cosmically cute idol, Mikado Nagi.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.380
We'll be taking the Uta☆Pri Award.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:10.100
Cutie Nagi, cutie Nagi, cutie Nagi!

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:10.100
It's no wonder they're expected to win the Uta☆Pri Award!

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:13.230
HE☆VENS' presence is overwhelming!

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:19.320
Let's see our second group of nominees, ST☆RISH!

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.030
We've got a broadcast!

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.240
What broadcast?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.740
Hi! I hope you're having a good morning this evening!

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.370
It's Tsukimiya Ringo! He's so cute!

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.000
Why do I have to do this?

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.750
ST☆RISH is currently visiting a campsite on their vacation.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:47.010
Look at how they're dressed. Do they even want to win?

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:50.560
Even without that, the difference between us is like heaven and hell.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.810
They're camping.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.770
Their composure will drive them into a corner.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:00.940
Good. How truly interesting.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.650
ST☆RISH, congratulations on your nomination.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.160
Tell us how you're feeling right now.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.490
Let's start with you, Nacchan.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:10.450
Natsuki.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.460
It's like a dream. I'm honored.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:22.710
Two groups have been nominated, but only one group will achieve glory!

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:25.380
The Uta☆Pri Committee has specially prepared a location

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:29.090
appropriate for a battle between these two groups!

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.140
A battle?

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:35.270
The battle is a concert showdown!

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:40.810
HE☆VENS seems like a formidable opponent. How do you feel about that?

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:44.780
We want to deliver our music to everyone.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.740
That's all.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:49.950
"We want to deliver our music to everyone," apparently.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.580
Do you believe you have a chance of winning?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.950
Of course.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.200
If we're doing it, we'll win.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.960
Do they not think anything of us?

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:05.090
Those honest eyes and pure hearts...

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.840
It's unbearable.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:11.510
ST☆RISH is just as confident!

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:23.190
The ST☆RISH standing here isn't the ST☆RISH you all know!

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.650
Allow me to introduce him!

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:30.240
Like a million volts, captivating all living things in the world,

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.160
he is the Mr. Mysterious Boy...

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.080
Aijima Cecil!

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:40.250
He is ST☆RISH's new member!

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:44.710
Look, look!

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.670
Who is that?

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.170
He's wonderful!

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:53.220
This is ST☆RISH's true form.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.140
What a surprise.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:59.770
The star symbol of ST☆RISH was the "A" of Aijima Cecil.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.900
The new, seven member group ST☆RISH.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:05.440
What kind of world will they show us?

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:09.360
No matter how many there are, it is the same!

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:11.860
He's here.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:13.950
What?!

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:18.910
An incredible person is here in the concert hall!

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:25.540
The intimidating creator of HE☆VENS, Raging Otori!

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:27.750
That's...

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:29.800
Raging Otori,

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:34.760
President of Raging Entertainment, the industry's greatest agency.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.390
Otori Eiichi...

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.980
Is that his father?

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.610
That guy's clearly extraordinary.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:49.530
It's been a while, Saotome.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:54.490
You don't seem to have changed.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:59.240
I have a suggestion for you today!

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:04.120
In order to determine who is the true Uta☆Prince,

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:08.590
we should conduct this contest under a certain condition!

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:15.140
Singing songs written by the same composer would be the best of the best.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.010
What?

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.970
The same composer?

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:24.940
I have here fantastic songs composed by Miss Nanami.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:30.900
Take whichever one you like, and arrange it however you please.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.110
What?

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:37.950
<i>Have you finished the new song for ST☆</i>RISH I requested?

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.370
<i>I wrote a few songs. If you would choose one of them...</i>

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:48.790
<i>That's great! Keep writing more songs.</i>

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:52.550
But I wrote those songs for everyone...

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.680
I was wondering what you would say.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:57.760
President!

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.060
It will only expose the difference in their strength.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:02.680
Very well!

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.690
Um, you can't just decide...

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.350
I'm saying we will do it!

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:13.320
This should be an interesting battle.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:17.110
What? This is really becoming crazy!

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:23.750
The groups will compete by singing songs written by the same composer!

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.580
The same composer?

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:31.500
A song can change dramatically depending on its arrangement.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.220
Listen, HE☆VENS!

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:39.800
If you lose this battle, you will be disbanded!

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:40.550
Is that clear?

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.470
How can he disband them?

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:48.650
Raging Entertainment has no need for losers.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:52.110
How harsh of Raging Otori!

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:56.110
His standard of perfection hasn't changed since he was an idol!

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:00.200
It won't change how overwhelmingly talented we are.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.070
Why not?

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.040
That's an unusually good idea.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.830
Disbanded, huh?

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:12.040
Good. I'm incredibly thrilled.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:20.390
In that case, if ST☆RISH loses, they will be disbanded as well.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:21.680
What?!

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.430
But...

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:27.560
Old man, are you sure you should be saying that?

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:30.480
No problem!

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:36.400
Laugh while you can, boy.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.570
Another surprise!

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:40.110
It seems both parties will participate in this competition

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.660
with their careers as idols on the line!

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.450
What? The losing group will disband?

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.740
But I'm a fan of both of them!

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.000
Please don't disband!

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:55.920
Who will become the most brilliant new idol group and win the Uta☆Prince Award?

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:57.760
A concert showdown for their careers!

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:01.930
We'll meet again in another special broadcast!

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:03.850
The announcement just concluded.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:05.890
Yes, we'll adjust our schedule.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:09.850
A contest between HE☆VENS and ST☆RISH should be interesting.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:15.020
On top of that, it's a battle of destiny between Raging Otori and Shining Saotome.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:17.320
Hey, change tomorrow's front page article!

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.320
Because of the Uta☆Pri Award,

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.110
we'll run a special article on HE☆VENS and ST☆RISH!

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:27.990
Those interested in attending the Uta☆Pri Award event,

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.910
tickets will go on sale at 10 o'clock.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:33.000
We will now distribute numbered tickets.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.250
ST☆RISH is in trouble.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.340
They don't stand a chance against HE☆VENS.

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:43.590
Shining, don't you think you've gone too far?

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.010
You're going to disband them?

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.510
They're still young.

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:52.560
Mister Kotobuki, are you that worried about them?

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:59.070
No, but no one wants to see their darling juniors sad.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:04.660
This world is not so easy that you can lose and expect to survive.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:07.080
Skill is everything.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:11.500
Do you not have faith in your juniors?

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:20.130
Amazing. There are pictures of us in the newspaper.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:22.630
The Uta☆Pri Award is on the front page.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:26.720
It's a rare title. It's big news.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:30.010
Congratulations on your nomination!

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:31.560
Tomo!

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.480
You even have a new member too.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:36.940
You guys are full of surprises.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.770
Anyway, have you seen this?

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:42.440
The presidents of our agency

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:45.990
and Raging Entertainment have always been rivals.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:50.330
I can't imagine that scary guy being an idol.

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:53.120
I looked it up out of curiosity,

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:57.210
but it seems he was the top idol before our president's big break.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:00.210
His masterpiece, "LOVE IS DEAD,"

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:04.340
sold 19 million copies, achieving the sales record of the time.

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:08.510
19 million? That's amazing.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:11.970
What? It's all written in there?

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:15.100
After his glorious retirement,

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:19.480
he was surpassed by the 20 million sales of our boss' "Because of Love."

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:21.650
Precisely.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:25.110
Destiny, is it?

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:29.280
Yeah, but we're the ones who will be battling.

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:30.530
That has nothing to do with it.

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:34.870
We should simply work to have our music heard by as many people as possible.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:39.000
And it's the debut of the new ST☆RISH with Cecil.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:42.710
You guys really are amazing.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.260
You don't seem like a group that's at risk of being disbanded.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:46.670
Of course we don't.

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:49.180
We've got Nanami on our side.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:52.430
That's right. Let's give it everything we have.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:53.720
Haruka?

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:56.770
I'm sorry.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:57.890
Are you okay?

00:13:58.640 --> 00:13:59.480
Yeah.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:00.270
Nanami.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.820
We won't lose. Believe in us.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:06.650
I will.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:10.450
Okay, let's do this!

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:11.700
Let's do it!

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.160
I'm excited!

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.110
Let's start by practicing!

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.790
They really are positive, aren't they?

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:21.380
Do they really think they can beat their opponents so easily?

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:23.340
At this rate, they'll be disbanded.

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:26.210
What's this? Ran-Ran, could it be you're sad?

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:28.170
I'm not sad at all.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:30.930
You're not honest, are you?

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:31.760
Shut up.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:34.720
But the probability of ST☆RISH winning is...

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:37.230
50%.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:40.100
That's higher than I expected.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.730
It's 50/50, huh?

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.650
Camus!

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.610
There you are.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.490
Thank you.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:58.450
When I returned to my country, you sent me the new song.

00:14:58.450 --> 00:15:00.210
It made me very happy.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.790
There's no way I would do something like that.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:08.380
I simply told him where he could reach you.

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:12.970
Kotobukii has persistently asked me for your contact information.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:15.390
I don't know why he used it.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.270
Camus.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:19.230
Regardless,

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.600
I can't believe royalty would abandon

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.150
the throne to become an idol.

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:27.070
I didn't abandon it. I had it postponed.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.360
It does not matter either way.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.860
You can't rely on others forever.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.490
I have nothing to do with you.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.240
Don't talk to me about this kind of thing.

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.490
You have everything to do with this.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:43.710
If not for you, I would not have become an idol.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:45.170
What do you mean?

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:49.670
You taught me the fundamentals of being an idol.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:52.930
It's all thanks to you.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:55.760
I simply performed my duties.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:57.470
That's fine.

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:01.520
I want you to know how grateful I am.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.810
Do whatever you want.

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.690
Then, goodbye.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:21.410
<i>And it's the debut of the new ST☆</i>RISH with Cecil.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:28.210
Something you can devote yourself to after giving up everything else, huh...

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:35.590
That was our first recording as seven, so I'm glad we had Nanami listen.

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:38.640
Let's go home and practice.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.020
Haru, I hope you'll watch our lesson too.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.480
I'm sorry, I...

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:47.060
You must be busy with your new song.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:48.230
Yes.

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:51.400
Arranging it must be hard, but do your best.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:52.820
I will.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:59.080
Well, well. You're all here.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.330
I've been wanting to meet you.

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:08.420
We're meeting ST☆RISH in person. I'm so moved.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:10.340
Nice to meet you.

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:13.920
I'm the universe's greatest idol, HE☆VENS' Mikado Nagi, 13 years old.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:14.840
I look forward to working with you.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.840
You're so small and cute.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:20.560
I look forward to working with...

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:26.190
Oh, come on. Did you think I'd really shake your hand?

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:27.230
You...

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:31.860
You're far too inexperienced to be challenging us.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.280
Isn't that right, Kira?

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:37.450
You're unpleasant.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:41.830
That's enough, Nagi. Let's go.

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:44.750
Why? Let's talk with them some more.

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:51.750
Hey, are you their manager?

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.750
What? I...

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:56.170
Haruka is ST☆RISH's composer!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:57.090
Huh?

00:17:57.880 --> 00:18:00.220
ST☆RISH's composer?

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:03.810
You're the one who wrote our new song?

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:08.600
Really? I had no idea this girl wrote that song.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:12.270
It is a very good song.

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:16.780
Oh, wow. Kira never talks this much.

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:21.240
ST☆RISH will disband soon...

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.160
At our hand.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.450
What will you do after you disband?

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:28.460
ST☆RISH will not lose!

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:35.420
You've got a nice look in your eyes.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:37.420
They're fantastic.

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:42.720
Become our composer.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:46.180
What are you doing?

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:46.520
Hey!

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:49.140
Why don't you take your hand off her?

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.940
I wanted to see those faces.

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:00.320
I can't stand it.

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.320
Let me see more.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.370
HE☆VENS, we're ready for you!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:10.080
Victory - and you - will definitely be ours.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.580
Definitely.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.500
Let's go, Kira.

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:25.470
Damn it! They really gave it to us!

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.770
I won't let them take Haruka!

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:28.890
Of course not!

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:31.850
We've got to win for Nanami!

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:32.850
Yes!

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:35.860
Let's continue where we left off yesterday.

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:56.340
<i>In that case, if ST☆</i>RISH loses, they will be disbanded as well.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:20:00.260
<i>Of course we don't. We've got Nanami on our side.</i>

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:03.930
<i>We won't lose. Believe in us.</i>

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.800
<i>Become our composer.</i>

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:11.810
We can't lose, no matter what.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:17.190
<i>The same composer?</i>

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:22.190
<i>A song can change dramatically depending on its arrangement.</i>

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:32.040
Um, here. This is for you.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.620
Thank you.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:36.040
Goodbye.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:53.270
<i>Ichinose, you're practicing so late.</i>

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:56.770
<i>Yes. There's an assignment I'm struggling with.</i>

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.270
<i>What assignment?</i>

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:03.490
<i>Could it be the song I sent you?</i>

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.740
<i>Don't worry about it.</i>

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:11.790
<i>This is my assignment. I will make it a song I can be proud of.</i>

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:15.850
<i>Songs are a mirror that reflect the heart.</i>

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:20.350
<i>You are already heading towards the next stage.</i>

00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:08.050
Don't take your eyes off us!

00:24:08.050 --> 00:24:09.300
Boredom is forbidden.

00:24:09.300 --> 00:24:10.620
Uta☆Pri.
